      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Inadvertent aortosaphenous vein graft-coronary vein anastomosis during coronary bypass surgery is an uncommon complication. We describe a case of aortosaphenous vein side-to-side anastomosis to an obtuse marginal vein resulting in a large arteriovenous fistula and elective closure, using embolization coils delivered percutaneously via the coronary sinus. The clinical findings, interventional procedure, and follow-up are also presented, with a discussion of alternative techniques used previously to treat iatrogenic aortosaphenous vein graft venous fistulae."},
